   184	    Transfer center colors between trail-selected bordered sprites, then crop to them.
   185	
   186	    Input structure:
   187	    - A full-size canvas contains several bordered sprites plus a grey (5) one-stroke trail.
   188	    - The trail's two endpoints connect, via sprite-colored port cells, to exactly two destination sprites.
   189	
   190	    Rule:
   191	    - Use the two trail endpoints to identify the destination sprites.
   192	    - For each destination, look up the sprite whose border color matches that destination's original center color, and copy that source center color into the destination center.
   193	    - Delete every non-destination sprite, erase the grey trail, then return only the minimal bounding rectangle covering the remaining destination sprites.
